{
  "title": "Session.fireCallback silently drops callbacks after 50ms lock \
timeout",
  "description": "Session.fireCallback uses callBackLock.tryLock with a 50ms \
timeout for every callback type except TABLE_CHANGE/DIALOG (5000ms) and logs a \
warning + drops the callback on timeout. GAME_UPDATE and MESSAGE callbacks to \
bridges and the spectator can therefore vanish under transient contention \
(e.g. a slow watcher view build holding the lock, concurrent chat broadcasts \
at game start). For the golden harness a dropped GAME_UPDATE can change what \
the bridge auto-pass loop observes, and a dropped update to the spectator \
loses event-log entries. The comment above the timeout claims game lifecycle \
callbacks are protected, which is true, but the 50ms tier is still a \
silent-drop design. Direction: per-session send queue with a dedicated writer \
(no drops, preserves order) or at minimum raise the short tier and make drops \
fail loudly in harness mode. Flagged independently by code survey and the \
wait-for-watching flake investigation.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "server",
    "golden-tests",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-07-01T18:40:00.000000-07:00",
